From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wavjaby <devaraja1945@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 07:14:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] util: include linux/fcntl.h for F_SEAL_* only with bionic

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Android userspace on glibc]
Patch-Reason: Mesa built for Android against glibc (ATL-next) takes the DETECT_OS_ANDROID path; glibc fcntl.h redefines struct flock & co. after the kernel uapi linux/fcntl.h, while bionic fcntl.h is built on it. glibc fcntl.h already declares F_ADD_SEALS / F_SEAL_* under _GNU_SOURCE, which Mesa sets.
---
SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
 src/util/os_memory_fd.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/util/os_memory_fd.c b/src/util/os_memory_fd.c
index dc55d99c4124bfb4a745fa3c15d586b374eb737c..963033b8396240d57ac08a6588389b56283b1866 100644
--- a/src/util/os_memory_fd.c
+++ b/src/util/os_memory_fd.c
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@
 
 #include "detect_os.h"
 
-#if DETECT_OS_ANDROID
+#if DETECT_OS_ANDROID && defined(__BIONIC__)
 #include <linux/fcntl.h>
 #endif
 
